  "note": "Independent source rejudgment against RFC 7606 Section 5.1: \"The MP_REACH_NLRI or MP_UNREACH_NLRI attribute (if present) SHALL be encoded as the very first path attribute in an UPDATE message.\" Read every tagged unit and its producer. Builder and parsed-split tests assert first type 14 with lower-code attributes present; wire payload construction asserts [14,1,2] for announcement and [15] for withdrawal. Same-context, cross-context, rebuilt forwarding, stored-route relay and raw export override tests compare concrete emitted attributes/body bytes, not a generic successful parse. The compliant-leading control checks backing-array identity rather than accepting an unnecessary copy. MPAttributesTrail still marks an MP attribute after another type, and reach-before-unreach; WriteMPAttributesFirst copies unreach, reach, then other attributes. writeOrdinaryUpdateBody applies this normalization to overrides before compliant splitting, and buildFwdBody handles both forwarding contexts. The newly argument-free exhaustive-ignore comment documents the narrow position-classification switch without changing its branches. These tests retain falsifiable MP-first assertions. Verdict enforced; no execution or current discrimination freshness is claimed.",
